      "message": "Functions like `write_flash` take a `const std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e\u0026`. This forces the caller to use a `std::vector`. If the caller has a C-array, a `std::array`, or wants to pass a subset of a vector, they have to copy data. `std::span` is a lightweight, non-owning view of contiguous memory.\n\n**Before:**\n\n```c\nint write_flash(uint32_t offset, const std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e \u0026data);\n\n// Calling with a chunk (forces an allocation/copy!):\nwrite_flash(addr, std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e(firmware.begin() + file_pos, firmware.begin() + file_pos + current_chunk));\n\n```\n\n**After:**\n\n```c\n#include \u003cspan\u003e\n\nint write_flash(uint32_t offset, std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e data);\n\n// Calling with a chunk (zero copies!):\nwrite_flash(addr, std::span{firmware}.subspan(file_pos, current_chunk));\n\n```",
