      "message": "In modern C++, raw C-arrays should be avoided because they decay to pointers easily (losing size information) and don\u0027t integrate well with standard algorithms.\n\n**Before:**\n\n```c\nuint8_t aes_key_[32] \u003d { 0 };\nuint8_t hash[32];\n\n```\n\n**After:**\n\n```c\n#include \u003carray\u003e\n\nstd::array\u003cuint8_t, 32\u003e aes_key_{};\nstd::array\u003cuint8_t, 32\u003e hash{};\n\n// You can easily pass this to span-accepting functions, or use .data() for legacy APIs:\nSHA256(data.data(), data.size(), hash.data());\n\n```",
